#!/usr/bin/env bash
# PreCompact hook: shorten the compaction summary when a session auto-handoff
# will be injected right after it.
#
# Claude Code appends this script's stdout to the compaction prompt verbatim as
# an "Additional Instructions" block (exit 0 = instructions, exit 2 = block
# compaction). Every compaction, auto or manual, is followed by the
# SessionStart(compact) hook (claude-handoff-takeoff) injecting this session's
# auto-handoff, so the summary is a secondary record and does not need the full
# nine-section reconstruction. Measured auto-compacts before this hook: 3.5k-5.3k
# summary tokens and 108-170s of dead time, against a ~700-token handoff that
# carries the same state.
#
# Emits nothing when no handoff exists for this session — then the summary is the
# only continuity and should stay thorough.
#
# Env:
#   CLAUDE_COMPACT_BRIEF_DISABLE   set to 1 to keep default summaries
set -uo pipefail

main() {
  local input session handoff_dir
  [[ "${CLAUDE_COMPACT_BRIEF_DISABLE:-0}" == 1 ]] && return 0

  input=$(cat) || return 0
  session=$(jq -r '.session_id // empty' <<<"$input" 2>/dev/null) || return 0
  [[ -n "$session" && "$session" != */* ]] || return 0

  handoff_dir=${XDG_STATE_HOME:-$HOME/.local/state}/claude/handoffs
  [[ -s "$handoff_dir/$session.md" ]] || return 0

  cat <<'EOF'
A session handoff document is injected immediately after this compaction by a
SessionStart hook. It already carries the next goal and immediate action, the
decisions and their reasoning, files touched, live state (dev servers,
background agents), test results, and unresolved errors. Do not spend output
reconstructing that here.

Treat this summary as the secondary record and keep it short:
- Hold the <analysis> block to at most 5 terse lines. It is stripped before the
  summary is used and never read, so length there is pure latency.
- Target 400-600 words inside <summary>; do not exceed 900.
- Keep every required section heading, but "None" or one line is fine wherever
  that is accurate.
- In Files and Code Sections give the path plus one clause on why it matters.
  Do not reproduce code, diffs, or file contents; the transcript path is in the
  continuation message when exact text is needed.
- In All user messages use one short line per message, still preserving any
  security-relevant or explicitly stated constraint verbatim.
- Favour the most recent work and anything still unfinished over a
  chronological recap of work already completed.
EOF
}

main
exit 0
